COMPILATION OF: E49H4

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49H4

   1 a 0000 E49H4:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P4] `nb >= na' -- BARE/BARE, WRITTEN-order weak, and
   4 a 0006      deliberately the SAME LOWERED operand order as F3's swap (nb
   5 a 0006      first, na second).  H-B-invis predicts H4 byte-equals the
   6 a 0006      E49F3 golden but module names: two DIFFERENT written spellings
   7 a 0006      collapsing to ONE object is a strong transfer test of the
   8 a 0006      ORDER law onto bare operands. */
   9 c 0006   dcl
  10 c 0006     1 rec,
  11 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  12 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  13 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  14 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  15 c 0006   if nb >= na then k = 1;
  16 c 001D   put list('K=', k);
  17 c 003F   stop;
  18 a 0042 end E49H4;

CODE SIZE = 0042
DATA AREA = 000C
FREE SYMS = 3888
END  COMPILATION
